      "content": "That proactive timing makes sense, thanks. I'm really trying to nail this down because I have a massive 36-hour deep-work window coming up for this project. \n\nSince it's such an extreme endurance test, I'm wondering if the 200mg \"overstimulation\" limit is more of a general rule for standard days, rather than for an elite-level sprint. If I'm looking to push the absolute efficiency frontier for a prolonged period—basically ensuring there is zero drop-off in receptor saturation—is there a more aggressive protocol for someone with high tolerance? \n\nLike, for an extreme high-load scenario, could I theoretically push those top-offs closer to 250-300mg if I'm pairing it with the L-Theanine to manage the jitters, or is there a hard physiological ceiling where the cardiovascular strain makes it unsafe regardless of the focus benefits?",
